msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up your workflow code to write logs, report errors to your local notebook, and save partial work when a job is canceled. To read these outputs from your local notebook, see [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow).\n"
msgstr "Configura el código de tu workflow para escribir registros, informar de errores a tu notebook local y guardar el trabajo parcial cuando se cancela un trabajo. Para leer estas salidas desde tu notebook local, consulta [Ejecutar un managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| In the workflow | In your local notebook |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| Write with a logger from the `logging` module, or call `print()`. | `job.logs()` returns the lines. |\n"
"| Raise an exception, or exit with a nonzero code. | `job.status()` returns `ERROR`, and `job.logs()` shows the traceback. |\n"
"| Call `send_error()`. | `job.error_message()` and `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` return the code, message, and details. |\n"
"| Call `save_result()` in a `SIGTERM` handler. | `job.result()` returns the partial result of a canceled job. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| En el workflow | En tu notebook local |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| Escribe con un logger del módulo `logging`, o llama a `print()`. | `job.logs()` devuelve las líneas. |\n"
"| Lanza una excepción, o termina con un código distinto de cero. | `job.status()` devuelve `ERROR`, y `job.logs()` muestra el traceback. |\n"
"| Llama a `send_error()`. | `job.error_message()` y `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` devuelven el código, el mensaje y los detalles. |\n"
"| Llama a `save_result()` en un manejador de `SIGTERM`. | `job.result()` devuelve el resultado parcial de un trabajo cancelado. |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write logs {#write-logs}"
msgstr "Escribir registros {#write-logs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything that the workflow writes to standard output or standard error goes to the job's logs. Read the logs with `job.logs()` while the job runs or after it ends.\n"
msgstr "Todo lo que el workflow escribe en la salida estándar o en el error estándar va a los registros del trabajo. Lee los registros con `job.logs()` mientras el trabajo se ejecuta o después de que termine.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up a logger {#set-up-a-logger}"
msgstr "Configurar un logger {#set-up-a-logger}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the `logging` module from the Python standard library. `logging.basicConfig()` writes to standard error, which reaches the logs without delay. The format in the following example adds a timestamp to each line:\n"
msgstr "Usa el módulo `logging` de la biblioteca estándar de Python. `logging.basicConfig()` escribe en el error estándar, que llega a los registros sin retraso. El formato del siguiente ejemplo añade una marca de tiempo a cada línea:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`level=logging.WARNING` hides `INFO` messages from other packages, and `logger.setLevel(logging.INFO)` keeps `INFO` messages for your own logger. `qiskit_ibm_runtime` sets its own level with the `QISKIT_IBM_RUNTIME_LOG_LEVEL` environment variable.\n"
msgstr "`level=logging.WARNING` oculta los mensajes `INFO` de otros paquetes, y `logger.setLevel(logging.INFO)` conserva los mensajes `INFO` de tu propio logger. `qiskit_ibm_runtime` define su propio nivel con la variable de entorno `QISKIT_IBM_RUNTIME_LOG_LEVEL`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`print()` also reaches the logs, but standard output is buffered, so printed lines might not appear until the job ends. If you use `print()`, pass `flush=True`.\n"
msgstr "`print()` también llega a los registros, pero la salida estándar usa búfer, por lo que las líneas impresas podrían no aparecer hasta que termine el trabajo. Si usas `print()`, pasa `flush=True`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: get_logger() from qiskit_serverless adds a [PUBLIC] prefix that Functions uses to split provider and user logs for Catalog Functions; custom workflow logs strip it. Tested with 0.37.0: its lines have no timestamp, and logger.exception() and exc_info=True drop the traceback (PrefixFormatter builds new records with exc_info=None). Confirm whether to recommend the standard logging module for custom workflows, or to fix get_logger(). */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the log level for each run {#set-the-log-level-for-each-run}"
msgstr "Definir el nivel de registro en cada ejecución {#set-the-log-level-for-each-run}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To debug one run without changing the code, pass the log level as an argument:\n"
msgstr "Para depurar una ejecución sin cambiar el código, pasa el nivel de registro como argumento:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, set the level of your logger from the argument:\n"
msgstr "Para habilitar esto, define el nivel de tu logger a partir del argumento:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the workflow has an [argument schema](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), declare `log_level` in it, for example as `{\"enum\": [\"DEBUG\", \"INFO\", \"WARNING\"]}`.\n"
msgstr "Si el workflow tiene un [esquema de argumentos](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), declara `log_level` en él, por ejemplo como `{\"enum\": [\"DEBUG\", \"INFO\", \"WARNING\"]}`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: decide what to log {#best-practice-decide-what-to-log}"
msgstr "Práctica recomendada: decide qué registrar {#best-practice-decide-what-to-log}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Log enough to reconstruct a run from its logs:\n"
msgstr "Registra lo suficiente para reconstruir una ejecución a partir de sus registros:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**At the start, log what the run received.** Log the backend name, the number of circuits, and the other settings that change between runs.\n"
msgstr "**Al inicio, registra lo que recibió la ejecución.** Registra el nombre del backend, el número de circuitos y los demás ajustes que cambian entre ejecuciones.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Log the start and end of each stage.** Use fixed messages that you can search for.\n"
msgstr "**Registra el inicio y el final de cada etapa.** Usa mensajes fijos que puedas buscar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Log iterations at a fixed interval.** For example, log a line such as `iteration 10/200, energy=-1.1000` every 10 iterations, instead of every iteration.\n"
msgstr "**Registra las iteraciones a intervalos fijos.** Por ejemplo, registra una línea como `iteration 10/200, energy=-1.1000` cada 10 iteraciones, en lugar de en cada iteración.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Log exceptions with `logger.exception()` inside an `except` block.** The line includes the full traceback, even if the workflow recovers from the error.\n"
msgstr "**Registra las excepciones con `logger.exception()` dentro de un bloque `except`.** La línea incluye el traceback completo, incluso si el workflow se recupera del error.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Turn off progress bars.** The logs store each refresh of a progress bar, such as one from `tqdm`, as a separate line. Pass `disable=True` to `tqdm`, or log at an interval instead.\n"
msgstr "**Desactiva las barras de progreso.** Los registros almacenan cada actualización de una barra de progreso, como la de `tqdm`, como una línea separada. Pasa `disable=True` a `tqdm`, o registra a intervalos en su lugar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Keep the logs small.** Do not log large data, such as every shot. A managed workflow keeps only the newest 50 MB of logs for each job.\n"
msgstr "**Mantén los registros pequeños.** No registres datos grandes, como cada shot. Un managed workflow conserva solo los 50 MB más recientes de registros de cada trabajo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Use the words \"error\" and \"exception\" only in messages about failures.** If a failed job did not [report its error](#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), the exception that `job.result()` raises contains only the log lines that include these words.\n"
msgstr "**Usa las palabras \"error\" y \"exception\" solo en mensajes sobre fallos.** Si un trabajo fallido no [informó de su error](#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), la excepción que lanza `job.result()` contiene solo las líneas de registro que incluyen estas palabras.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: report errors with send_error() {#best-practice-report-errors-with-send-error}"
msgstr "Práctica recomendada: informa de los errores con send_error() {#best-practice-report-errors-with-send-error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When the workflow raises an exception, the job ends with the `ERROR` status, and the traceback goes to the logs. A managed workflow does not store the error, even for a `ServerlessError`. `job.error_message()` returns `{}`, and the exception that `job.result()` raises contains only the log lines that include `error` or `exception`. Checks of argument types and ranges belong in an [argument schema](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), which rejects a bad run before the job starts.\n"
msgstr "Cuando el workflow lanza una excepción, el trabajo termina con el estado `ERROR` y el traceback va a los registros. Un managed workflow no almacena el error, ni siquiera para un `ServerlessError`. `job.error_message()` devuelve `{}`, y la excepción que lanza `job.result()` contiene solo las líneas de registro que incluyen `error` o `exception`. Las comprobaciones de tipos y rangos de los argumentos corresponden a un [esquema de argumentos](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), que rechaza una ejecución incorrecta antes de que comience el trabajo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Report every error that stops the workflow with `send_error()`, so that your local notebook gets a short error with a code and details:\n"
msgstr "Informa con `send_error()` de cada error que detenga el workflow, para que tu notebook local reciba un error breve con un código y detalles:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException` with the same text.\n"
msgstr "`job.result()` lanza una `QiskitServerlessException` con el mismo texto.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, raise `ServerlessError` where the error happens, and wrap the code of your entrypoint in a `try` block that sends any error with `send_error()`. A workflow adds this handler to Catalog Functions, but not to managed workflows:\n"
msgstr "Para habilitar esto, lanza `ServerlessError` donde ocurre el error y envuelve el código de tu punto de entrada en un bloque `try` que envíe cualquier error con `send_error()`. Un workflow añade este manejador a las Catalog Functions, pero no a los managed workflows:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Raise the error again.** The final `raise` keeps the traceback in the logs and ends the job with the `ERROR` status.\n"
msgstr "**Vuelve a lanzar el error.** El `raise` final conserva el traceback en los registros y termina el trabajo con el estado `ERROR`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Subclass `ServerlessError` to name a group of errors.** The handler sends the name of the class, such as `InputError`, as the `exception` field.\n"
msgstr "**Crea una subclase de `ServerlessError` para nombrar un grupo de errores.** El manejador envía el nombre de la clase, como `InputError`, en el campo `exception`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Other exceptions also reach the handler.** They get the code `1`, and their `repr()` becomes the message, such as `ValueError('bad shots')`.\n"
msgstr "**Otras excepciones también llegan al manejador.** Reciben el código `1`, y su `repr()` se convierte en el mensaje, como `ValueError('bad shots')`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: custom (user) workflows run their entrypoint directly through fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py (fleets_runner.py _upload_custom_image_entrypoint). Only provider jobs get the main.tmpl handler, which calls send_error() for an uncaught exception. Should custom jobs get the same handler? Tested with qiskit-serverless 0.37.0: a raised ServerlessError creates no ERROR event, and error_message() returns {}. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Report a problem and continue {#report-a-problem-and-continue}"
msgstr "Informa de un problema y continúa {#report-a-problem-and-continue}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`send_error()` does not stop the workflow or change its status, so you can also report problems that the workflow recovers from, such as each circuit that it skips:\n"
msgstr "`send_error()` no detiene el flujo de trabajo ni cambia su estado, por lo que también puedes informar de problemas de los que el flujo de trabajo se recupera, como cada circuito que omite:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` returns every error that the workflow reported, including the errors of a job that ended with the `DONE` status. See [Find the cause of an error](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-the-cause-of-an-error).\n"
msgstr "`job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` devuelve todos los errores que informó el flujo de trabajo, incluidos los errores de un job que terminó con el estado `DONE`. Consulta [Find the cause of an error](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-the-cause-of-an-error).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Pass numbers and strings in `args`.** `error_message()` shows only the first item of a list.\n"
msgstr "**Pasa números y cadenas en `args`.** `error_message()` muestra solo el primer elemento de una lista.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Check the return value.** If a workflow cannot store the error, for example because the code runs outside a job, `send_error()` writes the error to the logs and returns `False`.\n"
msgstr "**Comprueba el valor devuelto.** Si un flujo de trabajo no puede almacenar el error, por ejemplo porque el código se ejecuta fuera de un job, `send_error()` escribe el error en los registros y devuelve `False`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: confirm which error codes user workflows should use. Catalog Function codes come from the IBM Quantum error code registry, which might not apply to user workflows. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clean up when a job is canceled {#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled}"
msgstr "Limpia los recursos cuando se cancela un job {#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you cancel a job, the workflow sends `SIGTERM` to your entrypoint, uploads the final logs, and shuts down the environment. Without a handler, Python stops immediately, and `finally` blocks do not run. The workflow also tries to cancel the QPU jobs and sessions that the workflow started with `get_runtime_service()`. See [Cancel linked QPU jobs](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs).\n"
msgstr "Cuando cancelas un job, el flujo de trabajo envía `SIGTERM` a tu punto de entrada, sube los registros finales y apaga el entorno. Sin un controlador, Python se detiene de inmediato y los bloques `finally` no se ejecutan. El flujo de trabajo también intenta cancelar los jobs de QPU y las sesiones que el flujo de trabajo inició con `get_runtime_service()`. Consulta [Cancel linked QPU jobs](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To keep partial work, register a handler for `SIGTERM`. Your local notebook then gets the partial result from a canceled job:\n"
msgstr "Para conservar el trabajo parcial, registra un controlador para `SIGTERM`. Así, tu notebook local obtiene el resultado parcial de un job cancelado:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, add the handler at the start of your entrypoint:\n"
msgstr "Para habilitarlo, agrega el controlador al inicio de tu punto de entrada:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`sys.exit()` in the handler raises `SystemExit` in the code that is running, so `finally` blocks run before the script ends. The job still ends with the `CANCELED` status.\n"
msgstr "`sys.exit()` en el controlador genera `SystemExit` en el código que se está ejecutando, por lo que los bloques `finally` se ejecutan antes de que termine el script. El job sigue terminando con el estado `CANCELED`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep the handler short, because the workflow shuts down the environment soon after `SIGTERM`. For long runs, also save checkpoints, so that a later run can resume after a job fails or reaches the 24-hour limit. See [Best practice: checkpoint long jobs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs).\n"
msgstr "Mantén el controlador breve, porque el flujo de trabajo apaga el entorno poco después de `SIGTERM`. Para ejecuciones largas, guarda también puntos de control, de modo que una ejecución posterior pueda reanudarse después de que un job falle o alcance el límite de 24 horas. Consulta [Best practice: checkpoint long jobs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: confirm the time between SIGTERM and shutdown. The cancel is a Code Engine hard stop (fleets/handler.py cancel_job, cancel_processing_tasks=True), and the repo sets no grace period. Tested with qiskit-serverless 0.37.0, the real fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py, and docker stop: the handler runs, save_result() writes the result, and result() on a CANCELED job returns it (the result endpoint does not check the status). Confirm on Fleets that a result written in the handler reaches storage before the hard stop. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Próximos pasos {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow) to start a job and read its status, logs, and result.\n"
"- [Manage files across runs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) to save checkpoints that a later run can resume from.\n"
"- [Choose a compute profile](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles) to run your workflow with more CPU, memory, or GPU resources.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recomendaciones\">\n"
"- [Ejecuta un flujo de trabajo gestionado](/guides/run-managed-workflow) para iniciar un job y leer su estado, sus registros y su resultado.\n"
"- [Gestiona archivos entre ejecuciones](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) para guardar puntos de control desde los que una ejecución posterior pueda reanudarse.\n"
"- [Elige un perfil de cómputo](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles) para ejecutar tu flujo de trabajo con más recursos de CPU, memoria o GPU.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
